                <section id="4240917d-5d53-4eb7-ad9f-71431c41323b">
                    <name>Burst Mode</name>
                    <attributes>
                        <attribute>
                            <name>details</name>
                            <value>Burst Mode.  The HTAX switch supports a burst mode. When sending minimum sized packets over the HTAX, bubbles are introduced through the delay of the arbitration mechanism. To address this issue the HTAX supports burst mode. A single grant can be used to transmit multiple packets.  Each packet is framed by sot and eot signals. The grant is only released by the release_gnt signal.  The FUs need to define a maximum burst size (MBS). If a grant is given by a FU the FU must be capable to receive multiple packets as defined by the MBS. The FUs may define burst capability only for small or larger messages. The definition of the MBS and the exact behaviour is out of scope of this specification and is part of the higher layer protocol (HTOC).</value>
                        </attribute>
                    </attributes>
                    <subElements>
